  "summary_en": "AI Watch (European Commission) country page summarising Latvia's February 2020 national AI strategy: education and skills, AI adoption in the public and private sectors, research, networking, data infrastructure and regulation. Latvia relies on the EU product safety and liability directives, plans a new legal environment and regulatory sandboxes, and adopts the CEPEJ ethical guidelines.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Latvia's 2020 strategy aims to promote the uptake of AI across the economy, with a particular focus on public administration",
   "Relies on the EU product safety Directive 2001/95/EC and the product liability Directive 85/374/EEC, but seeks more clarity for AI goods and services",
   "Plans a new legal environment for AI and regulatory sandboxes",
   "Integrates AI into education and develops an online AI course modelled on Finland's Elements of AI",
   "Supports open data governance and HPC infrastructure; priority sectors include transport, justice, agriculture and translation"
